statement:
Fix the finite-field datum [def-weil-finite-field-fiber] $p,a,q,k_0,k$, a prime $\ell\neq p$, a finite extension $E/\Ql$ contained in the chosen algebraic closure $\Qlb$, an integer $n\geq1$ and a coefficient ring $\Lambda\in\{A_{E,n},\mathcal O_E,E,\Qlb\}$. Let $Y_0$ be a proper [def-weil-proper-morphism] $k_0$-scheme, put $Y=Y_0\times_{k_0}k$, $s=\Spec k$, and let $a_Y:Y\to s$ (proper), $g_Y:Y\to Y$, $g_s:s\to s$, the exchange maps $\operatorname{FrEx}_{Y,*}(M)$, $\operatorname{FrEx}_{Y,!}(M)$ [def-weil-frobenius-square-exchange] and the transports $\tau_M:\RGamma(Y,M)\to\RGamma(Y,Lg_Y^*M)$, $\tau_{c,M}:\RGammac(Y,M)\to\RGammac(Y,Lg_Y^*M)$ for $M\in D^b_c(Y,\Lambda)$ be those of [def-weil-frobenius-cohomology-transport], with $\RGamma(Y,-)=\operatorname{Fib}_s(Ra_{Y*}(-))$ and $\RGammac(Y,-)=\operatorname{Fib}_s(Ra_{Y!}(-))$ [def-weil-ordinary-compact-cohomology, def-weil-finite-coefficient-point]. Let $\kappa_M:Ra_{Y!}M\xrightarrow{\sim}Ra_{Y*}M$, natural in $M\in D^b_c(Y,\Lambda)$, be the identification of the compact-support direct image [def-compact-support-direct-image-detailed, def-weil-integral-rational-qbar-compact-support] with the derived direct image [def-weil-derived-direct-image] of [prop-weil-proper-compact-coincidence], computed with the compactification $Y\xrightarrow{\operatorname{id}}Y\xrightarrow{a_Y}s$, the base change of $Y_0\xrightarrow{\operatorname{id}}Y_0\to\Spec k_0$. Use this same identity compactification to construct $\operatorname{FrEx}_{Y,!}$ in [def-weil-frobenius-square-exchange] and hence $\tau_{c,M}$ in [def-weil-frobenius-cohomology-transport]. Then for every $M\in D^b_c(Y,\Lambda)$:

1. $\operatorname{FrEx}_{Y,*}(M)\circ Lg_s^*(\kappa_M)=\kappa_{Lg_Y^*M}\circ\operatorname{FrEx}_{Y,!}(M)$ as morphisms $Lg_s^*Ra_{Y!}M\to Ra_{Y*}Lg_Y^*M$;

2. $\tau_M\circ\operatorname{Fib}_s(\kappa_M)=\operatorname{Fib}_s(\kappa_{Lg_Y^*M})\circ\tau_{c,M}$ as morphisms $\RGammac(Y,M)\to\RGamma(Y,Lg_Y^*M)$; hence, for every integer $i$, $\mathrm H^i(\tau_M)\circ\mathrm H^i(\operatorname{Fib}_s\kappa_M)=\mathrm H^i(\operatorname{Fib}_s\kappa_{Lg_Y^*M})\circ\mathrm H^i(\tau_{c,M})$ on $H^i_c(Y,M)$.
